	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nD36GUylti9DStRwB",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 4, DX 12, IQ 1, HT 11, HP 4, WILL 8, PER 9, FP 11, SPEED 5.75, MOVE 5, DODGE 8, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nPbZ6bns_z1C3K5O0",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 13 (offense 20, protection -7), threat tier minor, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "nCXdcQg7HTy70DjbU",
			"text": "Swarming Bites: No attack roll and no active defense. Swarming Bites: 1d-3 impaling, Reach C. Everything in the swarm's hex is bitten, with no attack roll and no defence. Roll HT against the accumulated venom or lose the use of a limb to cramp and swelling."
		},
		{
			"id": "ndkjsdWyHW5KyWYXX",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/centipede-swarm.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "ninPh_AYhwqsQcoJD",
			"text": "Independent build total: -25 points of racial traits plus 0 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "no-1-O7-hsSg4GCtP",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Centipede Swarm (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nG0QnliispqwqsgXd",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "ng5G8bnza15xDorRP",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 5 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "ny6K7TuPMeRsmn3FA",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 5 (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "n1_W_CUXowWeYLky2",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "n03PI6v025TMcsRpb",
			"text": "One hex of swarm, which is where the Size Modifier comes from; no individual in it is larger than a finger."
		},
		{
			"id": "nxY8Lf8spAx_JqRH1",
			"text": "Damage is stated as literal dice rather than derived from ST. A swarm has no meaningful Strength — the injury comes from how many mouths are in the hex."
		},
		{
			"id": "nS1gN4z2VDEozpBR6",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
